WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.339 --> 00:00:02.922
(upbeat music)

00:00:12.221 --> 00:00:13.725
- [Voiceover] We are recreating
blockbuster movie posters

00:00:13.725 --> 00:00:14.725
with Asians.

00:00:15.581 --> 00:00:18.164
(techno music)

00:00:22.845 --> 00:00:24.541
- Maggie and I are going to be recreating

00:00:24.541 --> 00:00:27.101
the cover of Mr. And Mrs. Smith.

00:00:27.101 --> 00:00:28.483
There aren't many movie posters

00:00:28.483 --> 00:00:30.728
with Asians on them

00:00:30.728 --> 00:00:31.757
and even if they are,

00:00:31.757 --> 00:00:33.752
usually they're accompanied
by other people.

00:00:33.752 --> 00:00:34.963
- You know I just really
wanted to see Asians

00:00:34.963 --> 00:00:37.821
being represented as the
people that I know in real life

00:00:37.821 --> 00:00:39.720
who are a) bad ass,

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:41.197
b) like super smart,

00:00:41.197 --> 00:00:43.944
show that by recreating movie posters

00:00:43.944 --> 00:00:46.621
where we are the heroes for once

00:00:46.621 --> 00:00:47.837
instead of the sidekick.

00:00:47.837 --> 00:00:49.356
- I've never been described as sexy,

00:00:49.356 --> 00:00:51.421
never been described as suave before.

00:00:51.421 --> 00:00:53.064
People call me cute,

00:00:53.064 --> 00:00:54.797
friendly, and funny

00:00:54.797 --> 00:00:56.656
but like never sexy.

00:00:56.656 --> 00:00:59.594
The male lead and the romantic interest.

00:00:59.594 --> 00:01:03.165
- Angelina Jolie embodies
this perfect human being.

00:01:03.165 --> 00:01:05.299
She's sexy, she's smart, she kicks butt.

00:01:05.299 --> 00:01:07.882
(techno music)

00:01:11.034 --> 00:01:13.135
- Brad Pitt like to think I could even

00:01:13.135 --> 00:01:14.840
like share the same space with him

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:16.285
was absurd to me growing up

00:01:16.285 --> 00:01:17.517
but I'm gonna do it now

00:01:17.517 --> 00:01:18.584
and I'm gonna kill it.

00:01:18.584 --> 00:01:19.784
- Brangelina, we're coming for you.

00:01:19.784 --> 00:01:22.367
(techno music)

00:01:27.995 --> 00:01:29.117
- So today I'm doing the movie poster

00:01:29.117 --> 00:01:30.221
for Jurassic World.

00:01:30.221 --> 00:01:31.696
You know growing up you sort of

00:01:31.696 --> 00:01:33.355
look at the media and you
can relate to other people

00:01:33.355 --> 00:01:34.680
who don't necessarily look like you

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:36.279
but to wake up every morning

00:01:36.279 --> 00:01:37.273
and look in the mirror

00:01:37.273 --> 00:01:38.392
and just know you look one way

00:01:38.392 --> 00:01:40.156
and to look at the world around you

00:01:40.156 --> 00:01:41.912
and realize oh I don't
look like anyone else.

00:01:41.912 --> 00:01:43.720
Then that can be very isolating.

00:01:43.720 --> 00:01:46.019
It would have been nice
for me to sort of know that

00:01:46.019 --> 00:01:47.341
okay I'm not alone.

00:01:47.341 --> 00:01:49.197
I do have more aspirations.

00:01:49.197 --> 00:01:50.054
I can look outward

00:01:50.054 --> 00:01:51.799
and I can see that there
are so many different things

00:01:51.799 --> 00:01:53.680
that I could do or could done.

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:55.501
It would have just
allowed me to dream larger

00:01:55.501 --> 00:01:56.562
and there's a lot of perceptions tied to

00:01:56.562 --> 00:01:58.002
what it means to be an Asian

00:01:58.002 --> 00:01:59.479
that are not seen as desirable

00:01:59.479 --> 00:02:01.223
as leading person material.

00:02:01.223 --> 00:02:02.962
But we have Asian Americans who are not

00:02:02.962 --> 00:02:04.583
necessarily being written in

00:02:04.583 --> 00:02:06.423
based on assumptions about
what an Asian is or is not.

00:02:06.423 --> 00:02:09.006
(techno music)

00:02:12.701 --> 00:02:14.117
We just need roles that are human

00:02:14.117 --> 00:02:16.450
and are written to be human.

00:02:17.405 --> 00:02:19.988
(techno music)

00:02:25.079 --> 00:02:26.800
- Today I'm going to be Harry Potter

00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:29.261
in the Deathly Hollows
Part two movie poster.

00:02:29.261 --> 00:02:30.941
When I was told I would do that,

00:02:30.941 --> 00:02:32.823
I was like oh do you want
me to be Ronald Weasley

00:02:32.823 --> 00:02:35.314
and then I was told no
you're gonna be the lead.

00:02:35.314 --> 00:02:37.623
- Seeing three Asian like leads

00:02:37.623 --> 00:02:39.223
in a film is so cool.

00:02:39.223 --> 00:02:42.445
- I am a huge Harry Potter fan.

00:02:42.445 --> 00:02:45.078
There are two Indian characters

00:02:45.078 --> 00:02:47.197
that I remember in Harry Potter.

00:02:47.197 --> 00:02:48.717
I mean I loved reading
about them in the books

00:02:48.717 --> 00:02:50.002
and I loved that they existed.

00:02:50.002 --> 00:02:52.007
I obviously related to other characters

00:02:52.007 --> 00:02:53.021
in the book as well

00:02:53.021 --> 00:02:54.285
but they definitely stick to me

00:02:54.285 --> 00:02:56.477
as two that I really remember.

00:02:56.477 --> 00:02:57.981
- Growing up there was never
kind of that role model

00:02:57.981 --> 00:02:59.637
feeling in Hollywood

00:02:59.637 --> 00:03:02.781
because we look up to everybody
that we see in the media.

00:03:02.781 --> 00:03:04.925
- The only Asians I saw growing up

00:03:04.925 --> 00:03:06.802
was Jackie Chan and Jet Li.

00:03:06.802 --> 00:03:08.445
Even now there aren't
any blockbuster movies

00:03:08.445 --> 00:03:10.685
starring a Asian lead.

00:03:10.685 --> 00:03:12.802
It changes the perception
of a certain community

00:03:12.802 --> 00:03:14.162
to the rest of the world too.

00:03:14.162 --> 00:03:16.745
(techno music)

00:03:18.962 --> 00:03:20.503
- It's not like oh I only like them

00:03:20.503 --> 00:03:21.644
because they look like me,

00:03:21.644 --> 00:03:24.205
but it does kind of make you feel like

00:03:24.205 --> 00:03:25.500
oh like maybe I could do that.

00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:28.083
(techno music)

00:03:37.436 --> 00:03:39.999
- Today I'm doing the Mockingjay poster

00:03:39.999 --> 00:03:42.299
which I'm a little bit nervous about.

00:03:42.299 --> 00:03:43.900
Like thinking about how

00:03:43.900 --> 00:03:46.802
a Singaporian Chinese
American immigrant like me

00:03:46.802 --> 00:03:50.583
could one day be some sort
of Katniss Everdeen figure

00:03:50.583 --> 00:03:51.783
was impossible.

00:03:51.783 --> 00:03:54.125
It's not just about
putting people of color

00:03:54.125 --> 00:03:56.461
in situations where they aren't normally.

00:03:56.461 --> 00:03:58.903
It's about bringing a
diversity of perspective

00:03:58.903 --> 00:04:02.765
of culture of background
to every role in Hollywood.

00:04:02.765 --> 00:04:03.783
The culture that you grow up in

00:04:03.783 --> 00:04:06.082
it informs every decision that you make

00:04:06.082 --> 00:04:07.341
and as creative people,

00:04:07.341 --> 00:04:09.421
it informs all of our
creative decisions as well.

00:04:09.421 --> 00:04:11.442
As for mainstream American media,

00:04:11.442 --> 00:04:13.303
the lack of Asian identity

00:04:13.303 --> 00:04:16.365
is not just missing out
on a whole perspective

00:04:16.365 --> 00:04:18.002
and culture of people
who are willing to add

00:04:18.002 --> 00:04:19.223
to the conversation,

00:04:19.223 --> 00:04:20.861
it's doing a real injustice
to younger audiences

00:04:20.861 --> 00:04:24.861
who feel like that's something that they

00:04:24.861 --> 00:04:25.898
can never attain.

00:04:25.898 --> 00:04:27.341
When simply that's just not true.

00:04:27.341 --> 00:04:29.924
(techno music)

00:04:31.901 --> 00:04:33.085
Whatever they see on their screen,

00:04:33.085 --> 00:04:34.221
they can accomplish.

00:04:34.221 --> 00:04:35.581
They are interesting enough,

00:04:35.581 --> 00:04:36.605
they are talented enough.

00:04:36.605 --> 00:04:37.863
All we have to do is keep trying.

00:04:37.863 --> 00:04:40.446
(techno music)

00:04:46.845 --> 00:04:47.922
- Really it isn't that we necessarily

00:04:47.922 --> 00:04:49.461
need more of one thing.

00:04:49.461 --> 00:04:51.223
It's that we need more roles

00:04:51.223 --> 00:04:52.845
that are written in a multi-layered,

00:04:52.845 --> 00:04:53.901
multi-dimensional way.

00:04:53.901 --> 00:04:55.863
- I think I'm as sexy as Angelina Jolie

00:04:55.863 --> 00:04:57.180
and I believe it.

00:04:57.180 --> 00:04:58.823
- It's super important for us to

00:04:58.823 --> 00:05:00.461
encourage future generations.

00:05:00.461 --> 00:05:02.322
You're capable of doing great things.

00:05:02.322 --> 00:05:03.842
You are capable of doing this or that

00:05:03.842 --> 00:05:05.485
and you're worth it.

00:05:05.485 --> 00:05:06.925
- We might not be the
Katniss Everdeens today

00:05:06.925 --> 00:05:09.442
but it's going to happen.

00:05:09.442 --> 00:05:10.445
- You done?

00:05:10.445 --> 00:05:11.463
- Yes.

00:05:11.463 --> 00:05:12.583
(laughter)

00:05:12.583 --> 00:05:13.581
- All right ya'll.

00:05:13.581 --> 00:05:14.720
Well I'll see you tomorrow.

00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:15.725
Oh God.

00:05:15.725 --> 00:05:17.209
(laughter)

